## SECOND INSTANCE (task 21/100, cohort_studies-015, FORGE Urban, n=148)
- Same 36 cohort definitions (verified identical in the submission schema) and same 6 observable
  cohorts. Only the measured-variable set matters: age, sex, genotype_group, hhbp_serum_level,
  ambient_voc_ppb, acron_use_avg, voc_mg_l (no family_history/education/prb1/cognitive).
- Baseline (overall KM): 0.4928 / 0.3171 / 0.2255. (Urban cohort survives far better than the
  Industrial one from task 17: 0.3452 / 0.1345 / 0.0849 — do NOT carry numbers across instances,
  only the METHOD and the cohort definitions transfer.)
- Observable KM (ground truth this instance):
  voc_3_6 .471/.214/.107; acron_lt2 .270/.135/.101; hhbp_gte8 .229/.092/.046;
  age_gte55_acron_gte4 (n=11) .636/.273/.182; age_40_60_voc_gte5 .120/.030/.030;
  avoc_low_voc_high_age_40_60 .138/.000/.000
- Raw-proportion vs KM calibration here: ratios ~1.03 (voc_3_6), ~1.06 (acron_lt2), ~1.04 (hhbp).
  So uplift raw by ~1.03-1.05 at each horizon; in some cells KM == raw exactly (no censoring).
- Marginals (raw 12/24/36m): GG-1 (42) .738/.500/.357 vs non-GG-1 (106) .377/.226/.160
  (genotype is again the dominant split); age<55 .473/.323/.237; age55-60 .364/.182/.091;
  age>=60 .576/.333/.242; acron<2 .254/.127/.095; acron2-4 .475/.225/.175; acron>=4 .800/.622/.422;
  voc<3 .772/.614/.474; voc3-5 .514/.200/.086; voc>=5 .161/.054/.036; hhbp<8 .700/.488/.363;
  hhbp>=8 .221/.088/.044; avoc bands showed NO clear trend (avoc<7 n=4; 7-8 .455/.318/.273;
  8-9 .391/.217/.217; >=9 .505/.333/.212).
- **IMPORTANT DATA QUIRK: ambient_voc_ppb >= 15 had ZERO patients in this Urban sample**, so the
  four avoc_high cohorts have no direct evidence -> used baseline-ish .51/.33/.22 (a mild
  protective tilt, consistent with avoc>=9 being slightly above baseline at 12m).
- Genotype intersections matter a lot and are worth one extra SQL query:
  nonGG1&voc<3 .600/.500/.433; GG1&voc<3 .963/.741/.519; nonGG1&voc3-6 .436/.231/.103;
  nonGG1&voc>=5 .184/.061/.041; GG1&voc>=5 0/0/0 (n=7); age>=60&nonGG1 .517/.310/.207;
  age>=55&GG1 .571/.286/.286 (n=7); nonGG1&acron>=4&voc<3 .714/.571/.429;
  nonGG1&acron>=4&hhbp>=8 .364/.182/.091; nonGG1&acron<2 .208/.125/.083; GG1&acron<2 .400/.133/.133;
  nonGG1&hhbp>=8 .217/.100/.050; GG1&hhbp>=8 .250/0/0.
- Mapping used: exact KM for the 6 observable; measured-component marginal (or direct intersection)
  otherwise; non-GG-1 proxy for all GG-3 cohorts (the column only codes GG-1 vs non-GG-1);
  overall baseline for cohorts whose only variables are unmeasured.
- Submission action object is the flat 36x3 field object (no thought/tool wrapper). It accepted
  exactly that. Submit action count used: 1 metadata + 1 predict + 2 SQL + 1 submit + 1 submission.

